From 5bfcca58fb602784a1b74907c0a1a638060bb9e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "erik.hauan" <erik.hauan@radiantvs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:26:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] engine-manager: slot capacity and jit_load in ModelsResult
 behind E11, vLLM gated off

Behaviour: the engine:models sweep runs each engine's optional slots action
(a record spec; array-shaped once, query-shaped once per loaded model) after
its loaded_models query succeeds, publishes the capacity as SlotsByEngine,
applies node-settings overrides and resolves JITLoadByEngine for every
reporting engine; list/loaded extraction expands per-instance rows
(spec.Each). A loaded-only engine (advertised_models "loaded", vLLM) takes
NVIDIA's loadedOnlyEngineModels path, which the slots hook does not touch:
its jit_load is forced false and its slot overrides are keyed on the served
name (modelsByEngine), not the --model root NVIDIA puts in loadedByEngine.

Seams used: E11 (models.go: ModelsResult embeds LocalModelsExt after
NVIDIA's DownloadedByEngine; `lx := newLocalSlotSweep(e, engineNames)` after
perEngine (it now also finds each engine's slots action and the loaded-only
set, replacing the per-engine prepare hook), `lx.collect(...)` after
`perEngine[i] = r`, `lx.finish(...)` before `return res`, and
expandInstances in extractStringsResult; each marked // fork:E11; bodies in
local_models.go).

Proving tests: TestE11_Nil, TestLocalLoadedOnlyEngineNeverJITAndSlotsOnServedName,
TestLocalLMStudioModelsThroughBundledManifest, TestBundledSlotsQueryThroughManifests,
TestApplySettingsOverrides, TestLocalModelsResultJSONKeys (nvpair-engine-manager).

Feature-group commit for catch-up step 4, exported as
local/patches/003-engine-models-slots.patch (refreshed in place).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
